### API Gateway - resilience checks (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Parallel tests (rate limit, bulkhead, circuit breaker): scripts\resilience-tests.ps1

@gw = http://localhost:8080
@demoUserId = 7c9e6679-7425-40de-944b-e07fc1f90ae7

### 1. Circuit breakers + bulkheads right now
#    Circuit breakers appear after their route received the first request.
GET {{gw}}/actuator/resilience

### 2. Rate-limit headers - see X-RateLimit-Remaining / -Burst-Capacity / -Replenish-Rate
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/stock/LAP-APL-001/availability

### 3. Rate limit per USER: same request with X-User-Id uses that user's own bucket
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/stock/LAP-APL-001/availability
X-User-Id: {{demoUserId}}

### 4. /fallback is internal - called directly it is a 404
GET {{gw}}/fallback/product-read

### 5. Business errors are NOT failures: 404 passes through, the breaker stays CLOSED
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 6. Validation errors are NOT failures either (400 passes through)
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/users?size=500

### ---- With product-service STOPPED (read side down) ----

### 7. Search -> 503 fallback: "service": "product-read", "reason": "BACKEND_ERROR" / "CIRCUIT_OPEN", Retry-After: 15
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/products?q=laptop

### 8. Get by id -> 200 from the WRITE side, header X-Fallback-Source: product-write-service
#    Paste a product id (e.g. from GET http://localhost:8089/... or mysql-product)
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/products/PASTE-PRODUCT-ID

### ---- With order-service STOPPED ----

### 9. A WRITE that fails: 503 "Nothing was changed by this request." - and it is NOT retried
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{demoUserId}}

{ "userId": "{{demoUserId}}", "items": [ { "sku": "AUD-APL-001", "quantity": 1 } ] }
